<Project>

  <!--
    Deliberately empty, and deliberately present.

    MSBuild walks up from a project directory to the first Directory.Build.props it finds.
    Without this file the WiX installer project would inherit the repository root props, which
    exist for C# assemblies: TreatWarningsAsErrors, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, central package
    management and NuGet lock files all mean something to a csproj and nothing to a .wixproj,
    and central package management in particular breaks the WiX SDK's own implicit package
    references. Stopping the walk here keeps the packaging build independent of the Product
    build rather than coupling one to the other's compiler settings.

    The one thing the installer does share with the Product is its version, and that is imported
    explicitly from the root Directory.Build.props by the .wixproj so there is exactly one
    version source (SCRUM-11123 Part D).
  -->

</Project>
